{"seq":14,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T14:59:54.419Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"bd9ee751241785abcf4956b319a2f36bd80859d2fdb478933f5e7d49b32c7d45","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I can see (the North and Central team digests). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers turn up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk, Dock Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments for the 04:00 shift. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the shift cleared. The same note's action items also list a 6 Oct triage to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nA few things to know:\n• The two numbers use different formats (\"PD-\" prefix vs. none), so check against the ticket system before they go in the notes.\n• The 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal note both mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number.\n• The Central digests have tickets #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are on Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
